# Dashboard API client usage

All server-side API calls in the client dashboard must go through `@shipshout/api-client` `ApiClient` methods — not hand-built `fetch` URLs.

## Layering

| Layer | File pattern | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Transport | `shipshout.api.ts` (`ShipshoutApi`) | Cookie auth headers, `getApiClient()`, `getApiClientOptions()` |
| Domain API | `*.api.ts` (`AuthApi`, `ShoutoutsApi`, …) | Thin wrappers: `return api.someGeneratedMethod({ ...requestOptions, body, path })` |
| Server actions | `*.actions.ts` (`AuthActions`, …) | Form validation, redirects, `revalidatePath`; delegate to matching `*.api.ts` method |

## Do

```typescript
// shoutouts.actions.ts
static async publish(shoutoutId: string) {
  return ShoutoutsApi.publish(shoutoutId);
}

// shoutouts.api.ts
static async publish(shoutoutId: string) {
  const { api, requestOptions } = await ShoutoutsApi.getClient();
  return api.publishShoutout({ ...requestOptions, path: { id: shoutoutId } });
}
```

## Don't

- Call `ShipshoutApi.fetch('/shoutouts/...')` when `ApiClient` exposes the endpoint
- Put request/response mapping logic in `*.actions.ts` — keep actions thin
- Duplicate cookie/header building outside `ShipshoutApi`

## Exceptions

- **Set-Cookie handling** — read `result.response` and pass to `AuthUtils.applyToCookieStore` / `applyToNextResponse`
- **SSE streams** — use `parseAs: 'stream'` on the generated method, or `ShipshoutApi.fetch` when streaming needs raw `Response.body`
- **Endpoints not in OpenAPI** — add them to the Nest OpenAPI spec first, then regenerate; avoid permanent raw-fetch shortcuts

## Regenerate client

When an endpoint is missing or types are stale:

```bash
bun run openapi:generate
```

Requires the API serving OpenAPI at `http://localhost:8000/docs/openapi.json`. Run from repo root after spec changes.
